-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A: an ROR below a RAND is an island: it runs as before, so nothing commits (skeptic-design S3, S4, S5).
-- Pass: the answers before A, FULFILLED for sibling, doomed and violate.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF pa, pb, pc, pr
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF x, y, z, go, stop
-- (1) a doomed alternative: the RAND inside the left alternative is already
-- lost at 5, but b's act at 6 is a consumption by that alternative
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
doomed MEANS ((PARTY pa MUST x WITHIN 3) RAND (PARTY pb MAY y WITHIN 10)) ROR (PARTY pc MAY z WITHIN 10)
#TRACE doomed AT 0 WITH (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)   PARTY pb DOES y AT 6   PARTY pc DOES z AT 7
-- (2) a consumption by a SIBLING of the ROR, not by either alternative
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
sibling MEANS (PARTY pa MAY x WITHIN 10) RAND ((PARTY pb MAY x WITHIN 10) ROR (PARTY pc MAY z WITHIN 10))
#TRACE sibling AT 0 WITH PARTY pa DOES x AT 1   PARTY pc DOES z AT 2
-- (3) a violation versus an exercise, at one event
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
violate MEANS (PARTY pr SHANT go WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH) ROR (PARTY pr MAY go WITHIN 10)
#TRACE violate AT 0 WITH PARTY pr DOES go AT 1
